**Type:** Feature · **Repo:** `kbexplorer-template` · **Part of:** anokye-labs/kbexplorer-template#426 · **Blocked by:** anokye-labs/kbexplorer-core#18.

Render a rich-Markdown document with inline embedded blocks:
- a **block-renderer registry** modeled on the existing viewer registry;
- a `RichMarkdownDocumentView` composing frontmatter facts + prose + blocks;
- **reuse the existing inline-Mermaid** path as one block renderer;
- a **pre-built-SVG fallback** contract for blocks with no live renderer (replaces today's raw-code display at `ReadingView.tsx:368-371`);
- `dot` / `ics` / `canvas` renderers with fixtures.

**Acceptance:** the sample doc renders frontmatter in the structured view, a live Mermaid block, and a `dot`/`canvas` block via SVG fallback; no block falls back to raw code when an SVG exists; existing Mermaid tests still pass.

Requirements: anokye-labs/kbexplorer#12 (O2).

**Parent feature:** F0 — Create kbexplorer-search repo + package skeleton

## Scope
Define and export the core type contracts in `src/types.ts`:

```typescript
interface SearchUnit {
  nodeId: string;           // KBNode.id
  chunkIndex: number;       // 0 for single-chunk nodes
  text: string;             // searchable text content
  title: string;            // node title
  cluster: string;          // cluster id
  path?: string;            // source file path
  parentId?: string;        // hierarchy parent
  entityType?: string;      // structured node type
  identity?: string;        // canonical URN
  connections: string[];    // connected node IDs
  metadata: Record<string, unknown>; // extensible
}

interface EmbeddingVector {
  unitId: string;           // `${nodeId}#${chunkIndex}`
  vector: number[];         // embedding values
  model: string;            // model that produced this
  dimensions: number;
}

interface EmbeddingArtifact {
  version: number;
  generatedFrom: string;    // content hash of source graph
  model: string;
  dimensions: number;
  units: SearchUnit[];
  vectors: EmbeddingVector[];
}

interface SearchResult {
  nodeId: string;
  title: string;
  cluster: string;
  score: number;            // cosine similarity
  snippet: string;          // relevant text excerpt
  chunkIndex: number;
  path?: string;
  parentId?: string;
  identity?: string;
  entityType?: string;
  connections: string[];
  metadata: Record<string, unknown>;
}

interface SearchConfig {
  embedding: {
    provider: string;       // 'openai' | 'local' | 'custom'
    model: string;          // e.g. 'text-embedding-3-small'
    dimensions?: number;
    batchSize?: number;
  };
  artifacts: {
    dir: string;            // output directory for artifacts
  };
  chunking?: {
    maxTokens?: number;
    overlap?: number;
  };
}

interface EmbeddingProvider {
  name: string;
  embed(texts: string[]): Promise<number[][]>;
  dimensions: number;
}
```

Also inline a minimal subset of kbexplorer types (KBNode, KBEdge, KBGraph, Cluster,
Connection) in `src/kbexplorer-types.ts` with a TODO to switch to
`@anokye-labs/kbexplorer-core` when published.

## Validation criteria
Types compile, are exported from the barrel, and match the contracts described above.

## Evidence-based completion criteria
- [ ] `import { SearchUnit, SearchResult, EmbeddingArtifact } from "@anokye-labs/kbexplorer-search"` resolves
- [ ] Type definitions appear in `dist/*.d.ts` after build
- [ ] Inlined kbexplorer types have a TODO comment referencing kbexplorer-core

